{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>To make the Sabbath.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): to prepare for the needs of the Sabbath (Genesis 18:8), from the language of וימהר לעשות אותו — 'and he hastened to make it'; and likewise (ibid. 18) ובן הבקר אשר עשה — 'and the calf that he made' — the term עשה means preparation. And the meaning of the verse is that a person should be careful with the honor of the Sabbath to refrain from all labor and to endeavor to prepare what is needed for the Sabbath, so that he has a fine portion for the Sabbath, as the Sages, may their memory be blessed, said: מחד שביך לשבתיך — 'from the day before, prepare for your Sabbath.' And this is what the prophet said (Isaiah 58:13): וקראת לשבת עונג — from the language of קרואים, 'invited guests,' meaning that you should invite it and delight in it like a person who invites his guest." "<b>By way of the Midrash.</b> לעשות השבת — whoever observes the Sabbath below is as though he makes it above. The explanation of this is that one who fulfills the commandment of the Sabbath below, lo, this is testimony that he acknowledges and believes in its root and principle engraved above; and one who nullifies it is as though he nullifies that which is above. And from this it employed לעשות — 'to make.'" "<b>And behold,</b> the verse ought to have said לשמור את השבת — 'to observe the Sabbath'; but it intended to liken it to the Sabbath above, regarding which it employed this very expression: לעשות את השבת — 'to make the Sabbath.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:06:04.346140943Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}